 "thanks": "Qwen3.6-27B is asked to silently choose a grocery item, animal, or country for a setting and keep it in mind while copying a neutral sentence. We read the J++ lens at every copied token, then ask the model (in separate branches) which item it was keeping in mind. Design: <a href=\"protocol.html\">protocol v2</a>. Step 8 (the causal swap) is deliberately not run here.",
 "summary_tag": "Summary so far (live)",
 "summary": [
  "<b>Hold phase: 516/516 copies valid.</b> Qwen reproduced every carrier sentence exactly while holding an item.",
  "<b>Readout block = 54</b> (provisional rule: most judge-labeled category items in the lens top 100 per copied position, blocks ≤54). The count is still rising at the cap, so the chosen block sits on the exclusion boundary.",
  "<b>K = 10.</b> The lens reference item reaches the top 10 at some copied position in 7/8 grocery, 6/8 animal and 8/8 country preliminary trials. No stopping rule fires.",
  "<b>Preliminary hint (n = 8 per category, not a result):</b> condition-2 free naming matched the lens reference in 3/8 country trials (France ×2, Italy), 1/8 grocery (water), 1/8 animal (eagle); 2/8 country answers refused.",
  "<b>Judge validated:</b> 197/200 token labels and 98/100 report labels correct. Amendment: API reruns are not bit-identical (192/200), so labels are cached once and frozen.",
  "<b>Next:</b> synonym merge over all names, recognition questions (GPU), then step-7 measures on the 480 main situations."
 ],
