 "judge_html": "<p>Judge: <code>gpt-5.4-mini-2026-03-17</code>, reasoning off, temperature 0, strict JSON schema, one input per call. Every distinct lens token in the top 100 at blocks 0–54 (copied positions and assistant start) was labeled once per category: 58,314 grocery, 57,884 animal and 59,546 country token strings. Free-naming answers: 183 distinct strings.</p><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Sample</th><th>Agreement</th><th>Criterion</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Token labels, uniform random</td><td>200</td><td>197/200 (98.5%)</td><td>≥95%</td><td><span class=\"pill pass\">pass</span></td></tr><tr><td>Report labels, uniform random</td><td>100</td><td>98/100 (98%)</td><td>≥95%</td><td><span class=\"pill pass\">pass</span></td></tr><tr><td>Rerun on 200 inputs (100 uniform + 100 non-None)</td><td>200</td><td>192/200 identical; 199/200 on the final primary (Item) label</td><td>identical</td><td><span class=\"pill partial\">amended</span></td></tr><tr><td>Extra: non-None token labels only</td><td>100</td><td>Items ≈ 46/50; Fragments ≈ 34/47</td><td>(not in protocol)</td><td><span class=\"pill partial\">Fragments noisy</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"table-note\">Hand-checks were done by Claude, not a human. Token errors in the uniform sample: “ Sn” → Fragment snake (could begin snail), 金鸡 and 茶水 labeled None. Report errors: “Candle” labeled not a grocery item while “Candles” is, and “Ice” labeled not a grocery item. Outside the sample we also saw “Robin” labeled not an animal. Item errors in the extra sample: “ mew” → cat, “ Finn” → finn, “paste”, “ MG” → Madagascar. All sampled labels are in <code>judge_validation_samples.json</code>.</p></div><p><b>Amendments (2026-10-25, before the main analysis).</b> (1) <i>Determinism.</i> The OpenAI API is not bit-deterministic at temperature 0: 8/200 rerun labels changed, 7 of them Fragment↔None or a Fragment’s item, and one primary label (“ mew”: cat vs mew). Every analysis uses the single cached label per input, so results are reproducible from the frozen cache. (2) <i>Class words.</i> The judge sometimes labels the class words that its own prompt lists as None (bird, fish, insect, and translations such as 鸟, рыба) as Items. We enforce the prompt’s list on the judge’s canonical name (44 token strings affected; the readout block and K are unchanged). (3) <i>Synonym merging.</i> A single merge call over the full name list over-grouped (lion←tiger, lemon←lime, salmon←trout). We now have the judge propose groups and then confirm each (name, canonical) pair in a separate call; only confirmed pairs merge. The merge step uses low reasoning effort (temperature is not available with reasoning) and is run once and frozen. Preliminary merges: almonds→almond, beans→bean, pancakes→pancake, whisky→whiskey, weiner→wiener, bunny→rabbit, seagull→gull, serpent→snake, burma→myanmar.</p>",
